    hir_closure_digest_rekey_blocked_by_incomplete_interface_digest_2026-08-23, 0, "2026-11-27 p3sweep-20261127: the 2026-11-13 re-key landed but bcb9a5d64e9 then replaced the row scheme, leaving hir_cache_semantic_closure_digest_spec RED 2/6 at HEAD (alias-only registry remap digested EQUAL - stale-hit class; unfrozen/generation-misaligned surfaces digested instead of failing closed). Root cause: replacement rows rel|hash|len / rel|S:limbs / rel|C dropped the ordered registry mapping and all fail-closed validation. Fix (src/compiler/80.driver/driver_hir_cache.spl): hir_cache_closure_digest returns empty for unfrozen/zero-generation registries, torn ordered name/index mapping, surfaces with generation > registry.generation, or ordered indices outside the surface array; the ordered registry mapping (registry|name|index, exact order so all shard workers fold identical rows) is folded via a new defaulted third param on hir_cache_closure_digest_from_rows. Spec extended +3 contract rows; semantic closure digest spec 4/6 to 9/9 PASS; neighbours interface_keyed 11/11, closure_key 8/8, placeholder 5/5, worker_parity 14/14, skeleton 3/3, key_neutral 15/15, tldr_row_identity 4/4, differential 12/12 (69 rows, zero regressions). Residual: default closure key remains content rows (0% incremental hits) - flipping the default needs the shard-route placeholder-disagreement solved, a documented owner-lane decision; this fix completes the opt-in interface key. close_evidence reproducer=test/01_unit/compiler/driver/hir_cache_semantic_closure_digest_spec.spl prevention=test/01_unit/compiler/driver/hir_closure_digest_interface_keyed_spec.spl"

